{#
 The page that asks to confirm an unsubscribe, shown by the link of a mail. The link only shows this page: a mail scanner or a link
 preview that opens it must not unsubscribe anyone, so the change is made by the button, which posts to the same address.
 A theme writes its own as emails/subscription_confirm.html.twig (it gets: title, message, button).
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale|replace({'_': '-'}) }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
    <title>{{ title }}</title>
</head>
<body style="font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; display: flex; min-height: 100vh; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin: 0; padding: 20px;">
    <main style="max-width: 28rem; text-align: center;">
        <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
        <p>{{ message }}</p>
        <form method="post" action="">
            <button type="submit" style="padding: .6rem 1.4rem; font-size: 1rem; cursor: pointer;">{{ button }}</button>
        </form>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
